From b931fe9d6d5cf00bc55714ad3308d086f71850fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpovirk <cpovirk@google.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:47:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid eagerly allocating as much memory as a serialization
 payload requests.

See [the security advisory that this addresses](https://github.com/google/guava/security/advisories/GHSA-xxph-c9ww-hj94) (soon to be published as [CVE-2026-102554](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/cve-2026-102554)). We will publish a release 33.7.2 with the fix.

RELNOTES=`collect`: Changed `MapMaker`, `CompactHashMap`, and `CompactHashSet` deserialization to [avoid eagerly allocating as much memory as a serialization payload requests](https://github.com/google/guava/security/advisories/GHSA-xxph-c9ww-hj94).
PiperOrigin-RevId: 990274733
---
